# The native shell's build artefacts (issue #36).
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose. The repo root's .gitignore describes a
# no-build static site and should keep describing one.

# Capacitor's dependencies. The reason this whole directory exists is to keep
# these out of the repo root.
node_modules/

# THE webDir. Generated by ../tools/mobile/prepare-webdir.mjs on every build,
# and it is a COPY of index.html / app.js / styles.css / player/ / the runtime
# data subset. Committing it would create the second copy of the player that the
# prepare script's header exists to prevent: the site would get a fix and the
# committed copy would not.
www/

# ── The generated native projects ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `mobile/ios/` and `mobile/android/` are NOT ignored. Capacitor's own guidance
# is to commit them (they hold real project configuration — the Info.plist
# background-audio key, signing, the app icon set), and committing them keeps CI
# simple: no `cap add` step, no platform SDK needed to check out and build.
#
# Neither exists yet: nothing here has been generated, because neither platform
# can be BUILT on Windows and committing hundreds of unverifiable generated files
# is how a scaffold acquires a lie. See mobile/README.md § Generating the
# platforms. What IS ignored is what those projects produce when built.

# iOS
ios/App/App/public/
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/output/
ios/App/build/
ios/App/App.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
ios/App/App.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
ios/capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/

# Android
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json
# NOT ignored, deliberately, though Capacitor's own template ignores it:
#   android/app/src/main/res/xml/config.xml
# That is the Cordova-compat preference file, and it is where someone would set
# `KeepRunning="false"` to "save battery" — which calls the process-global
# pauseTimers() and stops every JavaScript out-point in the app firing.
# `tools/mobile/shell-invariants.test.mjs` parses it. An ignored file cannot be
# checked, so ignoring it would make that guard permanently dead.
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/
*.iml
*.apk
*.aab
